hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2671","Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Ala and Sa‘id ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman, both saying: Narrated to us Sufyan, from ‘Amr ibn Dinar, from ‘Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya‘la, from his father Ya‘la ibn Umayyah (RA), who said:\n\nI wished that I could see the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when the revelation descended upon him. When we were at al-Ji‘ranah, a man came to him wearing tattered clothes and heavily perfumed with perfume. He said, “I have entered into the state of ‘umrah, but I am wearing these clothes. What should I do?” So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him, “How did you used to act during your Hajj?” He said, “I would remove these clothes and wash them.” So he said, “Do the same for your ‘umrah as you would do for your Hajj.”\n\nThen revelation descended upon him, and he was covered with a garment. ‘Umar (RA) called me and uncovered the garment for me, so I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) snoring with his face reddened.\n\nThis is the narration of ‘Abd al-Jabbar.\n\nAl-Makhzumi said: He said, “We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) at al-Ji‘ranah, and I had said to ‘Umar (RA), ‘I wish I could see the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).’” And he said, “I would wash this perfume from myself.”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
